  "_note": "Task IDs carry a 'T' prefix corresponding to the bare numeric IDs in plan.md and the phase-spec headings (e.g. manifest 'T1.1.1' == spec 'Task 1.1.1'). MERGED PHASES: phases 3+4 are bundled under one manifest phase (phase 3, 'core-rest') and phases 6+7+8 under one (phase 6, 'feature-layers') so implement-hybrid runs their independent sub-phases concurrently (cross-phase task_groups share a wave). Group/task IDs keep their ORIGIN-phase prefix (3.x, 4.x, 6.x, 7.x, 8.x). The merged phase's spec_file is a ROUTER STUB (spec/phase-34-core-rest.md, spec/phase-678-feature-layers.md) that redirects each task ID to its authoritative original spec (spec/phase-3-*.md, phase-4-*.md, phase-6-*.md, phase-7-*.md, phase-8-*.md), which are unchanged. The stub is only consumed by the implementer/verifier prompt; review-spec's 'task ID exists in spec_file' invariant is therefore satisfied via the router redirect, not by inlining tasks. Wave ordering within a merged phase preserves each origin phase's internal chain; the two index.html appenders in the feature phase (7.5.a, 8.3.a) are split across waves 6.3 and 6.4 so no two implementers write index.html in the same wave.",
